  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1203 AM CDT THU AUG 27 2026\n\nThe radar is clear across Central Alabama at this time. However,\nthere is a cluster of storms over MS moving SEWD through the\nupper NW flow. In the upper levels we continue with a large ridge\nAZ/NM and into NRN Mexico and upper over ERN Canada extending SWD\ninto ERN Conus. This convection is expected to for the most part\ngo over MS and into portions of SRN AL. Hires guidance does show\na scattering of possible returns over the next few hours across\nCentral AL, generally S of the surface boundary (SRN half of\nCentral AL). Best chances for the remainder of the night will be\nacross our SW counties. With some more meanderings of our surface\nboundary today expected, our best chance of storms both Thursday\nand Friday will be across the S/SE portions of the area as\nanother wave/disturbance comes through the NW upper flow and\naround the base of the E Conus trough. Although our surface\nboundary is expected to fizzle out on Thursday, another boundary\nwill quickly move in to replace it from the NW on Friday. Upper\nridging is expected to expand EWD to much of the SRN US over the\nweekend. This in conjunction with surface ridging building across\nportions of the SE US will suppress some of the more widespread\nconvection this weekend into the remainder of the extended except\nfor the more isolated diurnally enhanced storms from the heat of\nthe day. We will not be looking at heat advisories just yet, heat\nindices will begin to creep back up as we progress through this\nweekend and into next week.\n\n08",
